Two loves I have, of comfort and despair,
That like two spirits do suggest me still.
My better angel is a man right fair, strong enough for bed
Against hard bondage; for as I play my fairest made dear,
Do you not consider that, unsparing a shake,
I bore him vexation; instead, I proved myself more late!
